{"reference":"Genesis 14","book":"Genesis","chapter":14,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The movement of Genesis","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Genesis moves from universal origins in chapters 1–11 to ancestral family narratives in chapters 12–50, ending with Jacob's household in Egypt. Genesis 14 belongs to that later ancestral movement rather than to the opening universal-origin section.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_014_ecef81e5fb79e4475098d295"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
